    "invocation_id": "e-6accf8c3-71e6-4a97-af84-746c3a9e3db8",
    "kind": "agent_answer",
    "from": "repair_agent",
    "text": "The issue is that in Python 3.11+, `netrc` returns an empty tuple `('', '', '')` for malformed entries instead of raising `NetrcParseError`. The existing code checks `if _netrc:`, which is true for `('', '', '')`, leading Requests to use empty credentials.\n\nThe fix is to ensure that we only proceed if there is actual login or password information present in the returned tuple.\n\nI have modified `src/requests/utils.py` to check for non-empty login or password fields before returning the netrc authentication tuple.\n\nThe change is:\n```python\n            _netrc = netrc(netrc_path).authenticators(host)\n            if _netrc and _netrc[0] or _netrc[1]:\n                # Return with login / password\n                login_i = 0 if _netrc[0] else 1\n                return (_netrc[login_i], _netrc[2])\n```\n\nI will now submit the patch."
  },
