    "text": "The repository issue regarding empty netrc entry usage has been fixed.\n\nIn `src/requests/utils.py`, the logic for processing netrc entries was updated to explicitly check for the presence of a username or password in the returned tuple from `netrc`. This ensures that empty or malformed netrc entries, which now return `('', '', '')` in Python 3.11+, are correctly ignored, restoring the intended behavior of the library.\n\nThe patch has been submitted."
